---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy & Data Handling | ImageLab"
  description="Read how ImageLab protects your files: 100% local on-device processing for core image, graphic & PDF tools, plus zero-storage transient encrypted processing for AI OCR."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-14 space-y-8 animate-fade-up">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 mb-2">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">
        Privacy Policy &amp; Data Handling
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-2">Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="studio-card rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">1. Local On-Device Tools (Zero Uploads)</h2>
        <p>
          All core image, graphic, and PDF utilities on ImageLab—including Image Converter, Image
          Compressor, Resizer, Visual Crop &amp; Rotate, Privacy Blur &amp; Redact, EXIF Metadata
          Remover, Batch Watermark, QR Code Generator, Barcode Generator, SVG to PNG, Favicon
          Generator, Color Palette Picker, Sign PDF, Organize &amp; Rotate PDF, Image to PDF, Merge
          PDF, Split PDF, Compress PDF, and PDF to JPG—execute entirely inside your browser using
          local memory and background workers. Your files never leave your device and are cleared
          automatically when you close or refresh the tab.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">2. Image to Text (AI OCR) Transient Processing</h2>
        <p>
          To provide fast, high-accuracy text extraction for English, Bengali, angled signs, and
          handwriting without requiring heavy multi-megabyte downloads, our{' '}
          <a href="/image-to-text" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Image to Text (OCR)</a>{' '}
          tool resizes your photo locally and sends it transiently over HTTPS to our serverless OCR
          endpoint, which forwards it to a cloud vision AI provider solely to return the recognized
          text. ImageLab does <strong>not</strong> save, log, or store your uploaded images or
          extracted text on any database or disk. Avoid submitting highly confidential credentials
          or legal IDs to cloud OCR if you require strictly offline processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">3. Local Storage &amp; Browser Data</h2>
        <p>
          ImageLab uses lightweight browser storage only for core functionality:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> Saved in <code>localStorage</code> so your Light or Dark mode choice persists.</li>
          <li><strong>Tool-to-tool handoff:</strong> When you click <em>Send to</em>, your file is stored temporarily in your browser’s local <code>IndexedDB</code> and deleted immediately once opened in the target tool.</li>
          <li><strong>Offline app shell:</strong> Our Service Worker caches static interface assets locally so pages load faster.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">4. Privacy-First Analytics, Hosting &amp; Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          ImageLab is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which processes standard transient network metadata
          (such as IP address and request headers) to protect against abuse and deliver pages
          globally. To understand aggregate traffic, countries, device types, and page speed,
          ImageLab may use cookieless, privacy-first analytics (such as Cloudflare Web Analytics or
          Umami). These tools do not set tracking cookies, do not fingerprint devices, and never
          record your file names or file contents. If Google AdSense is enabled in the future, this
          policy will be updated accordingly and any required consent controls will be presented.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">5. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or privacy inquiries? Reach out anytime via our{' '}
          <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
